 "_about": "Theme rules for sweep_bills.py. Added 11 November 2026 (Nathaniel: every bill is pulled into What's New and the horizon scan, with local, digital and visitor economy bills as the priority). A bill gets an advisor flag (Local, Digital, Visitor, the Policy Advisors' areas) if any pattern below matches its short title or long title. Flags label bills. They never decide whether a bill appears: What's New shows every bill that moved in the week. Patterns are case-insensitive regular expressions, so a word boundary is written \\\\b in this file. Add a billId to 'include' to force a bill into a theme the words miss, or to 'exclude' to drop a false match, with a reason. Check the 'matched words' list in bills.md each week. Edit this file, not the script.",
